<p id="S4.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx151" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{x}_{\max}:=\boldsymbol{x}\sigma_{S}\left(t\boldsymbol{x}^{\top}\right)=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}\exp(tx_{i})}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp(tx_{i})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{x}_{\max}:=\boldsymbol{x}\sigma_{S}\left(t\boldsymbol{x}^{\top}\right)=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}\exp(tx_{i})}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp(tx_{i})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex combination of <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{i}\}_{i\in[n]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{i}\}_{i\in[n]}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is easy to see that <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> upper bounds <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>. It suffices to find <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies the lower bound condition. We lower bound the softmax weights on <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx152" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex224"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex224.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex224.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\frac{\sum_{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{i})}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp(tx_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\frac{\sum_{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{i})}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp(tx_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex225"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex225.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{i})}{\sum_{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{i})+\sum_{i:x_{i}\neq x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{i})}{\sum_{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{i})+\sum_{i:x_{i}\neq x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex226"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex226.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{\sum_{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{\max})}{\sum_{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{\max})+\sum_{i:x_{i}\neq x_{\max}}\exp(t(x_{\max}-2))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{\sum_{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{\max})}{\sum_{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}}\exp(tx_{\max})+\sum_{i:x_{i}\neq x_{\max}}\exp(t(x_{\max}-2))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex227"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex227.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{n_{\max}}{n_{\max}+(n-n_{\max})\exp(-2t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{n_{\max}}{n_{\max}+(n-n_{\max})\exp(-2t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex228"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex228.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1+(\frac{n}{n_{\max}}-1)\exp(-2t)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1+(\frac{n}{n_{\max}}-1)\exp(-2t)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\max}:=\left|\{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}\}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\max}:=\left|\{i:x_{i}=x_{\max}\}\right|</annotation></semantics></math>. Choosing <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\frac{1}{2}\log(8n^{3/2}r^{\prime}P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\frac{1}{2}\log(8n^{3/2}r^{\prime}P)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx153" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex229"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex229.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex229.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{1+(\frac{n}{n_{\max}}-1)\frac{1}{8n^{3/2}r^{\prime}P}}\geq\frac{1}{1+\frac{1}{8r^{\prime}P\sqrt{n}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{1+(\frac{n}{n_{\max}}-1)\frac{1}{8n^{3/2}r^{\prime}P}}\geq\frac{1}{1+\frac{1}{8r^{\prime}P\sqrt{n}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.9.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we can lower bound <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx154" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex230"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex230.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{x}_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{x}_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex230.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq x_{\max}p_{\max}-2r^{\prime}(1-p_{\max})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq x_{\max}p_{\max}-2r^{\prime}(1-p_{\max})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex231"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex231.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{\max}-(x_{\max}+2r^{\prime})(1-p_{\max})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{\max}-(x_{\max}+2r^{\prime})(1-p_{\max})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex232"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex232.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq x_{\max}-4r^{\prime}\left(1-p_{\max}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq x_{\max}-4r^{\prime}\left(1-p_{\max}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex233"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex233.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq x_{\max}-4r^{\prime}\left(1-\frac{1}{1+\frac{1}{8r^{\prime}P\sqrt{n}}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq x_{\max}-4r^{\prime}\left(1-\frac{1}{1+\frac{1}{8r^{\prime}P\sqrt{n}}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex234"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex234.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{\max}-\frac{\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}}{1+\frac{1}{8r^{\prime}P\sqrt{n}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{\max}-\frac{\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}}{1+\frac{1}{8r^{\prime}P\sqrt{n}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex235"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex235.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq x_{\max}-\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq x_{\max}-\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.10.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}=\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}=\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the definition (<a href="#S4.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) shows that <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{x}_{\max}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{x}_{\max}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 19</span></span><span id="Thmlemma19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,n,N\in\mathbb{N}_{\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,n,N\in\mathbb{N}_{\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,\phi\in\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,\phi\in\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{X}^{(1)},\cdots,\boldsymbol{X}^{(N)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{X}^{(1)},\cdots,\boldsymbol{X}^{(N)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> input sequences that are tokenwise <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r,\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r,\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>-separated. Denote <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}=\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}n^{2}N^{2}\sqrt{\pi d}r\phi^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}=\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}n^{2}N^{2}\sqrt{\pi d}r\phi^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists a feedforward block <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(pjt)}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(pjt)}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> with depth <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, width <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{d,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{d,4\}</annotation></semantics></math> and weight bound <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}n^{2}N^{2}\sqrt{\pi d}r\phi^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}n^{2}N^{2}\sqrt{\pi d}r\phi^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx155" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex236"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex236.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(pjt)}\left(\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(pjt)}\left(\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex236.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma19.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma19.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}\subset\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}\subset\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> are non-negative and tokenwise <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2r^{\prime},2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2r^{\prime},2)</annotation></semantics></math>-separated. Moreover, for <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k,l\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k,l\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx156" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex237"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex237.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle{x}_{1,k}^{(i)}={x}_{1,l}^{(j)}\text{ if and only if }\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}=\boldsymbol{X}^{(j)}_{:,l}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> if and only if </mtext><mi>𝑿</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{x}_{1,k}^{(i)}={x}_{1,l}^{(j)}\text{ if and only if }\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}=\boldsymbol{X}^{(j)}_{:,l}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma19.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma19.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Furthermore, if <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\|\boldsymbol{X}_{:,k}\right\|_{2}\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\boldsymbol{X}_{:,k}\right\|_{2}\leq r</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(pjt)}\left(\boldsymbol{X}\right)_{1,k}\right|\leq 2r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(pjt)}\left(\boldsymbol{X}\right)_{1,k}\right|\leq 2r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma19.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the definition of the vocabulary</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex238" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex238.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\bigcup_{i\in[N]}\mathcal{V}^{(i)}=\left\{\boldsymbol{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\boldsymbol{v}=\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}\text{ for some }i\in[N],k\in[n]\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mtext> for some </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\bigcup_{i\in[N]}\mathcal{V}^{(i)}=\left\{\boldsymbol{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\boldsymbol{v}=\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}\text{ for some }i\in[N],k\in[n]\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}|\leq nN" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}|\leq nN</annotation></semantics></math>. We use Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma16" title="Lemma 16 ([], Lemma 13). ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> on <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> to find a unit vector <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{u}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{u}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx157" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n^{2}N^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{8}{\pi d}}\|\boldsymbol{v}-\boldsymbol{v}^{\prime}\|_{2}\leq\frac{1}{|\mathcal{V}|^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{8}{\pi d}}\|\boldsymbol{v}-\boldsymbol{v}^{\prime}\|_{2}\leq\left|{\boldsymbol{u}}^{\prime\top}(\boldsymbol{v}-\boldsymbol{v}^{\prime})\right|\leq\|\boldsymbol{v}-\boldsymbol{v}^{\prime}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mo>′</mo><mo lspace="0.222em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n^{2}N^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{8}{\pi d}}\|\boldsymbol{v}-\boldsymbol{v}^{\prime}\|_{2}\leq\frac{1}{|\mathcal{V}|^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{8}{\pi d}}\|\boldsymbol{v}-\boldsymbol{v}^{\prime}\|_{2}\leq\left|{\boldsymbol{u}}^{\prime\top}(\boldsymbol{v}-\boldsymbol{v}^{\prime})\right|\leq\|\boldsymbol{v}-\boldsymbol{v}^{\prime}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">for every <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{v},\boldsymbol{v}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{v},\boldsymbol{v}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{u}:=S{\boldsymbol{u}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{u}:=S{\boldsymbol{u}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}n^{2}N^{2}\sqrt{\pi d}\phi^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}n^{2}N^{2}\sqrt{\pi d}\phi^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(pjt)}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(pjt)}:\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx158" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex239"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex239.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(pjt)}(\boldsymbol{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(pjt)}(\boldsymbol{X})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex239.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\begin{pmatrix}\sigma_{R}\left(\boldsymbol{{u}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}+r^{\prime}\mathbf{1}_{1\times n}\right)\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\begin{pmatrix}\sigma_{R}\left(\boldsymbol{{u}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}+r^{\prime}\mathbf{1}_{1\times n}\right)\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx159" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}:=\sigma_{R}\left(\boldsymbol{{u}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}+r^{\prime}\mathbf{1}_{1\times n}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n},\quad i\in[N]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}:=\sigma_{R}\left(\boldsymbol{{u}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}+r^{\prime}\mathbf{1}_{1\times n}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n},\quad i\in[N].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N],k\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N],k\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, according to(<a href="#S4.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx160" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex240"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex240.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\boldsymbol{u}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}\right|=\left|S{\boldsymbol{u}}^{\prime\top}\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}\right|\leq S\left\|\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}\right\|_{2}\leq Sr\leq r^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mo>′</mo><mo lspace="0.222em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\boldsymbol{u}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}\right|=\left|S{\boldsymbol{u}}^{\prime\top}\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}\right|\leq S\left\|\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}\right\|_{2}\leq Sr\leq r^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Hence we can remove the ReLU activation in (<a href="#S4.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx161" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex241"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex241.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}=\boldsymbol{{u}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}+r^{\prime}\mathbf{1}_{1\times n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}=\boldsymbol{{u}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}+r^{\prime}\mathbf{1}_{1\times n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">It follows that for any <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[N],k,l\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[N],k,l\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx162" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex242"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex242.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left|{x}_{1,k}^{(i)}\right|\leq\left|\boldsymbol{{u}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}_{:,k}^{(i)}+r^{\prime}\right|\leq 2r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝑿</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|{x}_{1,k}^{(i)}\right|\leq\left|\boldsymbol{{u}}^{\top}\boldsymbol{X}_{:,k}^{(i)}+r^{\prime}\right|\leq 2r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx163" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex243"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex243.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|{x}^{(i)}_{1,k}-{x}^{(j)}_{1,l}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|{x}^{(i)}_{1,k}-{x}^{(j)}_{1,l}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex243.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\boldsymbol{u}^{\top}\left(\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}-\boldsymbol{X}^{(j)}_{:,l}\right)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\boldsymbol{u}^{\top}\left(\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}-\boldsymbol{X}^{(j)}_{:,l}\right)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex244"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex244.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=S\left|{\boldsymbol{u}}^{\prime\top}\left(\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}-\boldsymbol{X}^{(j)}_{:,l}\right)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mo>′</mo><mo lspace="0.222em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=S\left|{\boldsymbol{u}}^{\prime\top}\left(\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}-\boldsymbol{X}^{(j)}_{:,l}\right)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex245"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex245.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{S}{n^{2}N^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{8}{\pi d}}\left\|\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}-\boldsymbol{X}^{(j)}_{:,l}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{S}{n^{2}N^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{8}{\pi d}}\left\|\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}-\boldsymbol{X}^{(j)}_{:,l}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex246"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex246.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{S}{n^{2}N^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{8}{\pi d}}\phi\geq 2," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{S}{n^{2}N^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{8}{\pi d}}\phi\geq 2,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.9.1" class="ltx_text">where in the third step we make use of (<a href="#S4.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>). The above inequality also implies</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex247" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex247.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{x}_{1,k}^{(i)}={x}_{1,l}^{(j)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{x}_{1,k}^{(i)}={x}_{1,l}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p5.10.1" class="ltx_text">if and only if <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}=\boldsymbol{X}^{(j)}_{:,l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{X}^{(i)}_{:,k}=\boldsymbol{X}^{(j)}_{:,l}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 20</span></span><span id="Thmlemma20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N,n\in\mathbb{N}_{\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N,n\in\mathbb{N}_{\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}^{(1)},\cdots,\boldsymbol{x}^{(N)}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}^{(1)},\cdots,\boldsymbol{x}^{(N)}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a set of <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> input sequences that are non-negative and tokenwise <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2r^{\prime},2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2r^{\prime},2)</annotation></semantics></math>-separated. There exists a Transformer <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}:\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}:\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> with size <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(2,4),((2,3),(3,10))\times(n-1)\text{ times},(2,3),(2,4)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> times</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(2,4),((2,3),(3,10))\times(n-1)\text{ times},(2,3),(2,4)\}</annotation></semantics></math> and dimension vector <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}4\cdot\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times(n+2)}&amp;1\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}4\cdot\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times(n+2)}&amp;1\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex248" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex248.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)=z^{(i)}\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n},\quad i\in[N]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑻</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)=z^{(i)}\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n},\quad i\in[N],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma20.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma20.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{z^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{z^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following conditions:</span></p>
<ul id="S4.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any </span><math id="S4.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S4.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|z^{(i)}\right|\leq\frac{3\sqrt{2\pi}}{4}nN^{2}r^{\prime}+\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|z^{(i)}\right|\leq\frac{3\sqrt{2\pi}}{4}nN^{2}r^{\prime}+\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I4.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any </span><math id="S4.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> such that </span><math id="S4.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\neq\boldsymbol{x}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\neq\boldsymbol{x}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I4.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> up to permutations, </span><math id="S4.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|z^{(i)}-z^{(j)}\right|\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|z^{(i)}-z^{(j)}\right|\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I4.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="Thmlemma20.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma20.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The weight bounds of <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{FF}=\max\left\{2r^{\prime},\frac{3\sqrt{2}}{8}N^{2}\sqrt{\pi n}\right\},B_{SA}=\frac{1}{2}\log(3\sqrt{2\pi}n^{2}N^{2}r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{FF}=\max\left\{2r^{\prime},\frac{3\sqrt{2}}{8}N^{2}\sqrt{\pi n}\right\},B_{SA}=\frac{1}{2}\log(3\sqrt{2\pi}n^{2}N^{2}r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, if the first component of the input vector is replaced with any <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and the components of <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded by <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the components of the output of <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐓</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded by <math id="Thmlemma20.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{3\sqrt{2\pi}}{4}nN^{2}r^{\prime}+\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{3\sqrt{2\pi}}{4}nN^{2}r^{\prime}+\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}\in\mathbb{N}_{\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}\in\mathbb{N}_{\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of components of <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> that take different values. We define a new sequence <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bar{\boldsymbol{x}}^{(i)}\}_{i\in[N]}\subset\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bar{\boldsymbol{x}}^{(i)}\}_{i\in[N]}\subset\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> constructed as follows: for <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{x}_{j}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{x}_{j}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is taken as the <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th largest component of <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>; for <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}&lt;j\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}&lt;j\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{x}_{j}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{x}_{j}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then according to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma16" title="Lemma 16 ([], Lemma 13). ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, we can find a unit vector <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{{w}}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{{w}}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx164" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{8}{\pi n}}\left\|\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}-\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(j)}\right\|_{2}\leq\left|\left(\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}-\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(j)}\right)\boldsymbol{{w}}^{\prime}\right|\leq\left\|\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}-\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(j)}\right\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{8}{\pi n}}\left\|\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}-\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(j)}\right\|_{2}\leq\left|\left(\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}-\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(j)}\right)\boldsymbol{{w}}^{\prime}\right|\leq\left\|\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}-\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(j)}\right\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx165" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{{w}}:=P\boldsymbol{{w}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{{w}}:=P\boldsymbol{{w}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=\frac{3\sqrt{2}}{8}N^{2}\sqrt{\pi n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=\frac{3\sqrt{2}}{8}N^{2}\sqrt{\pi n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma18" title="Lemma 18. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, there exists a self-attention layer <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(max)}:\mathbb{R}^{3\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{3\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(max)}:\mathbb{R}^{3\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{3\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> with head number <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, head size <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> and weight bound <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\log(8n^{3/2}r^{\prime}P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\log(8n^{3/2}r^{\prime}P)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the condition in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma18" title="Lemma 18. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, there holds</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx166" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex249"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex249.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(max)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\widetilde{x}_{\max}\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒙</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒙</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(max)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\widetilde{x}_{\max}\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{x}_{\max}-\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}\leq\widetilde{x}_{\max}\leq{x}_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{x}_{\max}-\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}\leq\widetilde{x}_{\max}\leq{x}_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that, according to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 2 Proofs of Main Results ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, there exists a self attention layer <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}:\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}:\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}</annotation></semantics></math> satifsying the condition in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma18" title="Lemma 18. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx167" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{z}\end{pmatrix}\right):=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(max)}\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\\
\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(idt)}\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{z}\end{pmatrix}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\widetilde{x}_{\max}\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{z}\end{pmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒙</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒛</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒙</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒛</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒙</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒛</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{z}\end{pmatrix}\right):=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(max)}\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\\
\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(idt)}\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{z}\end{pmatrix}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\widetilde{x}_{\max}\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{z}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(idt)}:\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(idt)}:\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the self-attention layer from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma12" title="Lemma 12. ‣ 3.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ 3 Proof of Proposition : Construction of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> with head number <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, head size <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and weight bound <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. According to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ 2.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 2 Proofs of Main Results ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}</annotation></semantics></math> is of head number <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, head size <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> and weight bound <math id="S4.SS2.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\log(8n^{3/2}r^{\prime}P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\log(8n^{3/2}r^{\prime}P)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in[n-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in[n-1]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l}^{(sid)}:\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l}^{(sid)}:\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined as</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx168" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{y}\\
\boldsymbol{z}\end{pmatrix}\right):=\begin{pmatrix}\sigma_{R}\left(\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}(\boldsymbol{x})-2\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(elm)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{y}\end{pmatrix}\right)\right)\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}(\boldsymbol{z}+w_{l}\boldsymbol{y})\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{z}+w_{l}\boldsymbol{y}\end{pmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{y},\boldsymbol{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒙</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒚</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒛</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒙</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒚</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{y}\\
\boldsymbol{z}\end{pmatrix}\right):=\begin{pmatrix}\sigma_{R}\left(\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}(\boldsymbol{x})-2\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(elm)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{y}\end{pmatrix}\right)\right)\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}(\boldsymbol{z}+w_{l}\boldsymbol{y})\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{z}+w_{l}\boldsymbol{y}\end{pmatrix},\quad\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{y},\boldsymbol{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime}:=\begin{pmatrix}x_{1}^{\prime}&amp;\cdots&amp;x_{n}^{\prime}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}^{\prime}:=\begin{pmatrix}x_{1}^{\prime}&amp;\cdots&amp;x_{n}^{\prime}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math> having components</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx169" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x_{i}^{\prime}=\begin{cases}\sigma_{R}(x_{i}-2r^{\prime}),&amp;\text{if }|x_{i}-y_{i}|&lt;\frac{1}{2};\\
\sigma_{R}(x_{i}),&amp;\text{if }|x_{i}-y_{i}|&gt;1.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x_{i}^{\prime}=\begin{cases}\sigma_{R}(x_{i}-2r^{\prime}),&amp;\text{if }|x_{i}-y_{i}|&lt;\frac{1}{2};\\
\sigma_{R}(x_{i}),&amp;\text{if }|x_{i}-y_{i}|&gt;1.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
