</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Here, <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}:\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}:\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated from the ReLU FNN <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{FF}^{(idt)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{FF}^{(idt)}</annotation></semantics></math> in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma11" title="Lemma 11. ‣ 3.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ 3 Proof of Proposition : Construction of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> that implements the identity mapping and hence has depth <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, width <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and weight bound <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(elm)}:\mathbb{R}^{2\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(elm)}:\mathbb{R}^{2\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated from the ReLU FNN <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{FF}^{(elm)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{FF}^{(elm)}</annotation></semantics></math> in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma17" title="Lemma 17 ([], Lemma E.3). ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> and hence has depth <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, width <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> and weight bound <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{r^{\prime},2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{r^{\prime},2\}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th component of <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{w}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S4.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>). Therefore, <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l}^{(sid)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l}^{(sid)}</annotation></semantics></math> is of depth <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, width <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> and weight bound <math id="S4.SS2.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{2r^{\prime},P\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{2r^{\prime},P\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}:\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}:\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text"> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx170" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex250"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex250.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{y}\\
\boldsymbol{z}\end{pmatrix}\right):=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}(\boldsymbol{z}+w_{l}\boldsymbol{y})=\boldsymbol{z}+w_{n}\boldsymbol{y},\quad\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{y},\boldsymbol{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒙</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒚</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>𝒛</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{y}\\
\boldsymbol{z}\end{pmatrix}\right):=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}(\boldsymbol{z}+w_{l}\boldsymbol{y})=\boldsymbol{z}+w_{n}\boldsymbol{y},\quad\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{y},\boldsymbol{z}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">It can be seen that <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}</annotation></semantics></math> is of depth <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, width <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> and weight bound <math id="S4.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, our Transformer <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}:\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑻</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}:\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}\to\mathbb{R}^{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx171" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex251"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex251.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}:=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n-1}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\cdots\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,1}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑻</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{T}^{(sid)}:=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n-1}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\cdots\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,1}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N],l\in[n-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N],l\in[n-1]</annotation></semantics></math>, letting</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx172" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex252"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex252.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{l}^{(i)}:=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l-1}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\cdots\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,1}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{l}^{(i)}:=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l-1}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\cdots\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,1}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF}^{(idt)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{4\times n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">be the output of the <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th step of the <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th sample, we show inductively that</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx173" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex253"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex253.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{l}^{(i)}=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{l}^{(i)}=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation of <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated from <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> in the following way: when <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\leq{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\leq{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the first <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> largest components in <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> (where components with the same value are considered identical) are replaced by 0, while the remaining components remain unchanged; when <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l&gt;{n_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l&gt;{n_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}:=\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}:=\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is worth to note that <math id="S4.SS2.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{l}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the condition in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma18" title="Lemma 18. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the conclusion holds for the input obviously. Suppose that the conclusion holds for <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l={l^{\prime}}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l={l^{\prime}}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{l^{\prime}}\leq n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{l^{\prime}}\leq n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, since the largest value of <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bar{x}}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bar{x}}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>, by the induction hypothesis and (<a href="#S4.E21" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>)(<a href="#S4.E22" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx174" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex254"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex254.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex254.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\left(\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\left(\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex255"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex255.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime}-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime}-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex256"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex256.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime}-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime}-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex257"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex257.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}\left(\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}\right)_{1,:}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime},n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}\left(\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}\right)_{1,:}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime},n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\boldsymbol{x}^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2r^{\prime},2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2r^{\prime},2)</annotation></semantics></math>-separated and all components are non-negative, we know that <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}</annotation></semantics></math> is also <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2r^{\prime},2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2r^{\prime},2)</annotation></semantics></math>-separated with all components being non-negative from its definition. Therefore, the <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>-approximations <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> differ from the maximum component <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bar{x}}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bar{x}}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> by less than <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, while differing from all other components of <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> by more than <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. According to (<a href="#S4.E23" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx175" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex258"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex258.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}\right)_{1,:}=\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}\right)_{1,:}=\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{l^{\prime}}&gt;n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{l^{\prime}}&gt;n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, noticing <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}=\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}=\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, by the induction hypothesis and (<a href="#S4.E21" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>)(<a href="#S4.E22" title="In Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Lemma : Realizing Contextual Mapping by Transformers ‣ 4 Proof of Lemma : Memorization of Transformers ‣ Standard Transformers Achieve the Minimax Rate in Nonparametric Regression with 𝐶^{𝑠,𝜆} Targets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx176" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex259"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex259.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex259.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\left(\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\left(\boldsymbol{Z}_{l^{\prime}-1}^{(i)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex260"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex260.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime}-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime}-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex261"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex261.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime}-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,l^{\prime}}^{(sid)}\left(\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime}-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex262"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex262.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime}-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime}-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex263"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex263.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime},n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}_{l^{\prime}}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{l^{\prime},n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the induction is completed and we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx177" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex264"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex264.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{n-1}^{(i)}=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}_{n-1}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{n-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{n-1}^{(i)}=\begin{pmatrix}\boldsymbol{x}_{n-1}^{(i)}\\
\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\\
\boldsymbol{0}_{1\times n}\\
\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{n-1,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">From the definition of <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}</annotation></semantics></math>, it can be seen that <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{Z}_{n}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{Z}_{n}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> only outputs the aggregated summation information. Therefore, through an analysis similar to the one above, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx178" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex265"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex265.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{n}^{(i)}=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\left(\boldsymbol{Z}_{n-1}^{(i)}\right)=\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{n,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}=z^{(i)}\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓕</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{Z}_{n}^{(i)}=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{FF,n}^{(sid)}\circ\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}_{SA}^{(sid)}\left(\boldsymbol{Z}_{n-1}^{(i)}\right)=\left(\sum_{j=1}^{\min\{n,n_{i}\}}w_{j}\widetilde{\bar{x}}_{j}^{(i)}\right)\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n}=z^{(i)}\boldsymbol{1}_{1\times n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p12.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p12.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(i)}:=\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}\boldsymbol{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒘</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(i)}:=\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}\boldsymbol{w}</annotation></semantics></math>, with each component of <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2P\sqrt{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>-approximating the corresponding component of <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>. We now check that <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{z^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{z^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\frac{3\sqrt{2\pi}}{4}nN^{2}r^{\prime}+\frac{1}{2},2\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\frac{3\sqrt{2\pi}}{4}nN^{2}r^{\prime}+\frac{1}{2},2\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-separated. Let <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, noting that <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\boldsymbol{w}^{\prime}\|_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\boldsymbol{w}^{\prime}\|_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\boldsymbol{{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\boldsymbol{{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}\right\}_{i\in[N]}</annotation></semantics></math> are tokenwise <math id="S4.SS2.p12.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2r^{\prime},2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2r^{\prime},2)</annotation></semantics></math>-seperated, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx179" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex266"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex266.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|{z}^{(i)}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|{z}^{(i)}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex266.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}\boldsymbol{{w}}\right|=P\left|\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}\boldsymbol{{w}}^{\prime}\right|\leq P\left\|\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒘</mi></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}\boldsymbol{{w}}\right|=P\left|\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}\boldsymbol{{w}}^{\prime}\right|\leq P\left\|\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex267"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex267.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq P\left\|\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}-\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}\right\|_{2}+P\left\|\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq P\left\|\boldsymbol{\widetilde{\bar{x}}}^{(i)}-\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}\right\|_{2}+P\left\|\boldsymbol{\bar{x}}^{(i)}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex268"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex268.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq P\cdot\frac{\sqrt{n}}{2P\sqrt{n}}+P\cdot 2r^{\prime}\sqrt{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq P\cdot\frac{\sqrt{n}}{2P\sqrt{n}}+P\cdot 2r^{\prime}\sqrt{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex269"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
